From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:33:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] build: USCL_VIDEO_CORE_LTO, ThinLTO for video_core only

A whole-program ThinLTO build crashed Switch Sports Resort once on
"this == GetCurrentThreadPointer(kernel)": the core's guest threads are
fibers that resume on other host threads, and a thread_local read inlined
across files can be reused from before the switch. The GPU threads, where
racing time goes, have no fibers, so only video_core gets ThinLTO (clang,
link with lld -flto=thin).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/video_core/CMakeLists.txt | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/CMakeLists.txt b/src/video_core/CMakeLists.txt
index 590ba5bed..1668ae51b 100644
--- a/src/video_core/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/video_core/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -466,6 +466,14 @@ if (ENABLE_OPENGL)
 endif()
 
 target_link_libraries(video_core PUBLIC common core)
+
+# USCL_VIDEO_CORE_LTO=ON (clang + lld): ThinLTO for the GPU threads' code only. Not for core: its
+# guest threads are fibers that resume on other host threads, and thread_local reads (the current
+# KThread) inlined across files there can be cached from before the switch.
+option(USCL_VIDEO_CORE_LTO "ThinLTO for video_core only (clang, link with lld -flto=thin)" OFF)
+if (USCL_VIDEO_CORE_LTO)
+    target_compile_options(video_core PRIVATE -flto=thin)
+endif()
 # Shader precache builder: game archives use zstd (also with dictionaries) and zlib.
 target_link_libraries(video_core PRIVATE zstd::zstd ZLIB::ZLIB)
 target_link_libraries(video_core PUBLIC shader_recompiler stb bc_decoder gpu_logging)
